@startuml flowchart
title AI-Trade — How It Works (newcomer flowchart)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4D6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EAF4FF

|GitHub Actions|
start
:Cron fires
(daily: Mon–Fri after US close,
 weekly: Saturday morning);
note right
  Two triggers 30 min apart.
  The second is a safety net;
  re-runs never duplicate rows or orders.
end note
:Check out repo, install requirements;
:python -m predictors.daily_predict
or  predictors.weekly_predict;

|Predictor (predictors/*)|
:Load settings
config/common.toml + config/<job>.toml
(API keys come from env / GitHub Secrets);
:Build PredictionJob and call
common.pipeline.run(job);

|Pipeline (common/*)|
:Download macro data from Yahoo
(VIX, SPY, bonds, dollar, gold);
if (All macro series found?) then (no)
  #FFDDDD:Fail the run
  (nothing written);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

repeat :Next ticker (e.g. ^GSPC, AAPL, NVDA, MSFT);
  :Download ~5 years of daily prices
  (Alpaca or Yahoo);
  :Compute features
  (momentum, volatility, volume, RSI, MACD,
   VIX, market regime, cross-asset ...);
  :Train a fresh XGBoost model
  on the last ~3 years;
  :Predict the latest day:
  UP or DOWN + confidence;
  :Turn it into a signal
  index: BUY / SHORT (inverse ETF)
  stock: BUY / CASH;
repeat while (More tickers?) is (yes)
-> no;

:Open the prediction log CSV
(data/predictions.csv or
 data/weekly_predictions.csv);
:Back-fill old predictions whose horizon has passed:
actual direction, return, Correct = Yes/No;
:Append today's predictions
(skip if Date + Ticker already logged);
:Print accuracy & P&L per ticker,
trade checklist, GitHub job summary;

if (auto_trade on AND data source = Alpaca?) then (yes)
  |Alpaca|
  :Read account, positions, open orders;
  if (Open orders readable?) then (yes)
    :For each ticker:
    sell the side we should not hold,
    buy the side we should hold
    (equal budget per ticker, idempotent order IDs);
  else (no)
    :Skip all trading (safety);
  endif
else (no)
endif

|GitHub Actions|
if (CSV changed?) then (yes)
  :git commit "Predictions YYYY-MM-DD"
  and push to main;
else (no)
endif

|Dashboard|
:GitHub Pages index.html reads the CSVs
from main and shows signals, accuracy,
and confidence charts;
stop

@enduml
